      "rationale": "Frame: whole-plant fixed. The laser driver does not replicate per module; the 1 GWe plant requires one shared driver array (~500 beamlines) costing $2,000M in total. C220104 is a Class U account — the framework multiplies the per-module value by n_mod=10 to reach the fleet cost. Dividing by n_mod ($2,000M / 10 = $200M/module) ensures the fleet total stays at $2,000M rather than scaling to ~$20B. Marvel's driver uses ~500 femtosecond DPSSL beamlines at kJ-class energy and 10 Hz. LLNL IFE driver cost target: <$1.5B for a GW-class plant (osti-servlets-purl-15013230 §Introduction). Marvel's femtosecond CPA architecture uses a less mature manufacturing base (Ti:sapphire-class gain media, CPA gratings) with no established IFE-scale production — applying a 1.3–2× technology immaturity premium over the LLNL benchmark. Midpoint: $1.5B × 1.33 ≈ $2,000M fleet. Sensitivity range: $1,500M–$3,000M. At 500 beamlines this implies $3–6M per beamline (NOAK), consistent with LLNL analysis showing diodes account for 33–50% of beamline cost at IFE scale (osti-servlets-purl-3008974 §Section 3). Note: This override replaces the library's $/J-based driver calculation, which cannot capture the femtosecond CPA architecture.",
